1
00:00:00,244 --> 00:00:02,193
Olivia opens the signed deal.

2
00:00:02,525 --> 00:00:08,685
She needs dates, contacts, products, deliverables, approvals, assets, and destination

3
00:00:08,685 --> 00:00:09,190
links.

4
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:12,732
A handoff that says only sold one hundred fifty thousand

5
00:00:12,732 --> 00:00:14,951
dollars leaves the delivery team guessing.

6
00:00:15,978 --> 00:00:19,976
Michael explains that campaign dates may be finalized after signing.

7
00:00:20,295 --> 00:00:24,061
Separate the commercial close from operational handoff readiness.

8
00:00:24,406 --> 00:00:27,679
That lets the sale remain valid while making missing delivery

9
00:00:27,679 --> 00:00:30,620
information visible before the next stage begins.

10
00:00:31,685 --> 00:00:34,533
Agree the minimum prerequisites with both teams.

11
00:00:34,836 --> 00:00:37,859
A helpful validation rule can explain what is missing at

12
00:00:37,859 --> 00:00:38,576
handoff.

13
00:00:38,905 --> 00:00:42,454
An internal task can route work when readiness is confirmed.

14
00:00:42,757 --> 00:00:46,931
Legitimate exceptions need an agreed path rather than invented dates.

15
00:00:47,968 --> 00:00:50,200
The advertiser supplies materials.

16
00:00:50,494 --> 00:00:53,448
Relevant specialists review and prepare them.

17
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:57,968
The customer gives required approval, Client Success coordinates, and Ad

18
00:00:57,968 --> 00:01:00,059
Operations implements and tests.

19
00:01:00,391 --> 00:01:02,082
Timelines depend on the product;

20
00:01:02,337 --> 00:01:06,644
exact current lead times must come from the applicable guidelines.

21
00:01:07,687 --> 00:01:13,182
An advertiser cannot simply request undisclosed promotional material that imitates

22
00:01:13,182 --> 00:01:14,447
independent reporting.

23
00:01:14,770 --> 00:01:19,955
The process must preserve branding requirements, disclosures, and authorized review.

24
00:01:20,278 --> 00:01:24,992
Automate routing and documentation while keeping the necessary decision maker

25
00:01:24,992 --> 00:01:25,671
accountable.

26
00:01:26,706 --> 00:01:30,472
If a link fails, campaign specialists investigate delivery.

27
00:01:30,804 --> 00:01:34,812
If Salesforce repeatedly exports a stale link, the analyst may

28
00:01:34,812 --> 00:01:37,276
investigate the mapping with technical owners.

29
00:01:37,582 --> 00:01:41,191
Understanding the boundary helps fix the right system and prevent

30
00:01:41,191 --> 00:01:42,817
the same failure recurring.
